sn22.1:16.2 | S: They’re not obsessed with the thought: ‘I am perception, perception is mine!’ | T: (none)
sn22.1:16.3 | S: So when that perception of theirs decays and perishes, | T: (none)
sn22.1:16.4 | S: it doesn’t give rise to sorrow, lamentation, pain, sadness, and distress. | T: (none)
