sn22.1:17.4 | S: it doesn’t give rise to sorrow, lamentation, pain, sadness, and distress. | T: (none)
sn22.1:18.1 | S: They don’t regard consciousness as self, self as having consciousness, consciousness in self, or self in consciousness. | T: “He doesn’t assume consciousness to be the self, or the self as possessing consciousness, or consciousness as in the self, or the self as in consciousness.
sn22.1:18.2 | S: They’re not obsessed with the thought: ‘I am consciousness, consciousness is mine!’ | T: He is not seized with the idea that ‘I am consciousness’ or ‘Consciousness is mine.’
sn22.1:18.3 | S: So when that consciousness of theirs decays and perishes, | T: As he is not seized with these ideas, that consciousness changes & alters.
